                <invention-title lang="de">NETZWERK (NW)-VERFAHREN FÜR EINSCHRÄNKUNGEN BEI DER GLEICHZEITIGEN VERWENDUNG VON NETZWERK-SLICES</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="fr">TECHNIQUES DE RÉSEAU (NW) POUR CONTRAINTES SUR L'UTILISATION SIMULTANÉE DE TRANCHES DE RÉSEAU</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="en">NETWORK (NW) TECHNIQUES FOR CONSTRAINTS ON SIMULTANEOUS USE OF NETWORK SLICES</invention-title>
            </bibliographic-data>
            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>Techniques discussed herein facilitate configuration of network slices for a User Equipment (UE) supporting constraints on simultaneous operation of slices. receiving a registration request message to request registration on a set of requested network slices; registering the UE to a set of allowed network slices; and generating a registration accept message for transmission indicating the UE is registered to the set of allowed network slices, wherein the registration accept message indicates slice compatibility information for each allowed network slice of the set of allowed network slices for the UE, wherein the slice compatibility information for each allowed network slice indicates whether or not other configured network slices of a set of configured network slices are compatible with the configured network slice for simultaneous operation by the UE.</p>
            </abstract>
